  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member replying from the floating composer, I want the smiley picker to open and stay open on the first tap, so that I can insert a smiley without the composer collapsing and sending me back to the conversation. (Operator feedback on the latest iPhone build, 2026-11-15.)\n\n### Observed (operator, 2026-11-15, MP and topic)\n\n1. In an MP or a topic, tap Reply: the **floating composer** opens (the modern composer of #888, which is not yet behind its switch).\n2. Tap the smiley icon **the first time**:\n   - the smiley view opens, then closes almost at once;\n   - the user is back on the MP or topic, the keyboard hidden, and the composer **collapsed and stuck to the bottom of the screen**.\n3. The **second tap works**: the picker opens and stays.\n\n### Expected\n\nThe first tap opens the smiley picker, and it stays open until the user picks a smiley or dismisses it. The composer keeps its state (open, text, cursor), and the keyboard comes back when the picker closes.\n\n### Scope and order\n\n- This belongs to the **experimental modern composer** (#904, « Composer moderne »).\n- **Treat it after #903** has moved the composer to `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/ModernComposer/`, so the fix lands in its final place.\n- Check whether the legacy full-screen path (#855) shows the same problem once it exists.\n- Likely area, to confirm while fixing (no cause asserted here): the sheet or picker presentation racing with the keyboard dismissal or the composer's detent on the first presentation.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The first tap on the smiley icon opens the picker and it stays open, in an MP and in a topic, on iPhone (and on iPad if the same composer is used).\n- [ ] Closing the picker returns to the composer in its previous state (open, text and cursor kept).\n- [ ] A hosted UI test reproduces the first-tap case and is shown to fail before the fix.\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- #903\n\n### Precision (operator, 2026-11-15, corrected)\n\n- The composer **expanded to full screen** (the ↗ button of today's composer) does **not** show this problem: its smiley view stays open from the first tap.\n- The bug is limited to the **floating (compact) presentation**.\n\nSo the smiley-view presentation of the full-screen mode is the working one. When #903 moves the composer:\n- reuse that path for the floating mode, with one implementation shared by both modes, and do not keep two;\n- check the legacy full-screen path of #855 against it too.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
